From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - BRepFill_TrimSurfaceTool::IntersectWith
 throws NotDone on an incoherent intersection in a Release build

IntersectWith evaluates the bisector's intersection parameters with each of the two profile
edges' parallel faces and requires the two sequences to have the same length, then indexes the
second by the first's length. The requirement is StdFail_NotDone_Raise_if, which No_Exception
(set by CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release) empties, so in a Release kernel the mismatch is unchecked and
Points2.Value(i) reads past the end of a shorter sequence: an uncatchable SIGSEGV from
BRepOffsetAPI_MakeEvolved on a circular spine with a profile that starts on the circle's axis.

The check is now a literal throw, as the other two StdFail_NotDone sites in this file already are,
so the constructor reports a catchable StdFail_NotDone as the source documents.
---
 .../TKBool/BRepFill/BRepFill_TrimSurfaceTool.cxx   | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKBool/BRepFill/BRepFill_TrimSurfaceTool.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKBool/BRepFill/BRepFill_TrimSurfaceTool.cxx
@@ -389,8 +389,12 @@
   EvalParameters(EdgeOnF1, myFace1, myBis, Points);
   EvalParameters(EdgeOnF2, myFace2, myBis, Points2);

-  StdFail_NotDone_Raise_if(Points.Length() != Points2.Length(),
-                           "BRepFill_TrimSurfaceTool::IntersectWith: incoherent intersection");
+  // A literal throw: the _Raise_if macro is empty in a Release (No_Exception) build, and the loop
+  // below indexes Points2 by Points' length.
+  if (Points.Length() != Points2.Length())
+  {
+    throw StdFail_NotDone("BRepFill_TrimSurfaceTool::IntersectWith: incoherent intersection");
+  }

   gp_Pnt PSeq;
   int    NbPoints = Points.Length();
